stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> DESIGN_NEEDED

    DESIGN_NEEDED --> ka_plan: ka-workflow invokes ka-plan
    ka_plan --> ADR_GATE: route == COMPLEX_MODE
    ka_plan --> LOCKED_DECISION: route != COMPLEX_MODE

    ADR_GATE --> LOCKED_DECISION: 🛑 user approves ADR
    ADR_GATE --> DESIGN_NEEDED: user rejects, back to ka-plan

    LOCKED_DECISION --> ka_execute: ka-workflow invokes ka-execute\n(no preset action - reads decisions.json itself)

    state ka_execute {
        [*] --> ReadHandoff
        ReadHandoff --> ValidateSchema
        ValidateSchema --> RiskTierConfirm: 🛑 tier 1-4 confirmation
        RiskTierConfirm --> RouteToWorker
        RouteToWorker --> [*]
    }

    ka_execute --> BE_REVIEW_GATE: action == backend
    ka_execute --> DEPLOY_RESULT: action == ops
    ka_execute --> BUILD_DONE: action in [frontend, schema, test]

    BE_REVIEW_GATE --> BE_FE_GATE_ON_UI: 🛑 user approves walkthrough\n(needs UI)
    BE_REVIEW_GATE --> BUILD_DONE: 🛑 user approves walkthrough\n(no UI needed)

    BE_FE_GATE_ON_UI --> ka_execute: 🛑 approved, ka-execute runs frontend action

    state DEPLOYMENT_GATE_choice <<choice>>
    BUILD_DONE --> DEPLOYMENT_GATE_choice
    DEPLOYMENT_GATE_choice --> DEPLOYMENT_GATE: ops action needed

    DEPLOYMENT_GATE --> ka_execute: 🛑 workflow-level approve\n(then ka-execute tier-4 confirm again)
    ka_execute --> DEPLOY_RESULT

    DEPLOY_RESULT --> COMPLETION_GATE: success
    DEPLOY_RESULT --> BLOCKED: failure, retries exceeded

    COMPLETION_GATE --> READY_TO_ARCHIVE: 🛑 user confirms completion

    BLOCKED --> ka_execute: user runs --reset-retries\n(max 3x per state)
    BLOCKED --> DESIGN_NEEDED: 4th failure -\nreturn to ka-plan instead of retrying

    READY_TO_ARCHIVE --> [*]

    note right of ka_execute
        ka-execute owns all risk-tier
        confirmation + schema validation.
        ka-workflow never bypasses this.
    end note

    note right of BLOCKED
        Reset cap prevents infinite
        retry loops (added in 5.0.0).
    end note
